/-!
# The fixed Held two-subgroup and its orbit reachability

The exact closure of the eight published words is a two-group: a checked
normalizing sequence gives cyclic extensions of two-power order. Explicit
words carry a representative of every label fiber to each of its vertices,
so two vertices with the same label are conjugate under the seed action.

These certificates use the literal ATLAS HeG1-p2058B0 carrier, with no Held
order, simplicity, or Sylow assumption. Sources: GLS3 Table 5.3p and the
retained seed words and one-based orbit lists in `Source/`.
-/
